preConditionHook:
// EL: avgRange = average(h - l, rangeLookback)[2] -- the mean bar range
// over the rangeLookback bars ENDING ONE BAR BEFORE the signal bar, so the
// huge bar is not inside its own benchmark. Average recomputes from scratch
// every bar (EL_Summation_Probe, 2,808/2,808), so this is a FRESH loop and NOT
// the WFSafe_AvgTrueRange rolling accumulator. h - l is a price
// expression with real history, not an EL variable, so the loop reads price
// directly -- contrast BarRangeAboveStd, which has to mirror a variable's
// zero-filled warm-up. Summed newest-first, EL's Summation order.
avgRange = 0.0;
for (int i = 0; i < (int)rangeLookback; ++i) {
    avgRange += high[2 + i] - low[2 + i];
}
avgRange /= (int)rangeLookback;
